    "about": "The menu fields agent/menu.ts reads by name, for every live instance of the class each one names, and how frida_tools.menu_lines prints them. Each entry's kind says how the field is read: an entry with no kind is an enum and carries its word table; int and bool are plain values; string_array and enum_array are arrays, and an enum_array takes its words from the entry its words_from names. A field declared on a parent class names that class in declared_in. Each entry gives the line of the Il2CppDumper dump of the build below that the field, its class and its enum type were read from; tests/test_frida_tools.py checks those lines, and that each kind matches the type the dump gives, when the dump is on this machine. menu_lines prints the fields in the order listed here. The player-screen fields are private and have obfuscated names, so a new build needs this file read again from its dump. The plan is docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-30-ch-mcp-in-game-input.md, \"Menus without seeing\" and task K4.",
